'''Tainted Lost''' is a [[Characters|character]] added in [[The Binding of Isaac: Repentance]]. It is the alternate version of {{c|The Lost}}. Tainted Lost is unlocked by reaching {{s|Home}} and using the {{I|Red Key}}, {{P|Cracked Key}}, or {{P|1=Soul of Cain}} to access a special room in one of the walls while playing as the Lost.

Tainted Lost is similar to The Lost, but instead of {{i|Holy Mantle}}, it starts with a {{p|Holy Card}}; it also does not start with the {{i|Eternal D6}}. Like the Lost, Tainted Lost has [[flight]] and [[spectral tears]], but no health.

It also starts with a 1.3x damage multiplier, giving it higher starting damage and making most damage ups more powerful. Certain items will be automatically rerolled while playing as Tainted Lost, including most defense-oriented items (see [[Tainted Lost#Item Exclusion|Item Exclusion]]). To offset the lack of {{I|Holy Mantle}} and limited defensive options, all [[Cards and Runes|cards]] that spawn have roughly a 10% chance of being turned into a {{P|Holy Card}}.

== Notes ==
* Just as the Holy Mantle effect from the Holy Card negates damage taken in the first place, items such as {{I|Birthright}}, {{t|Missing Poster}} and {{P|Soul of Lazarus}} will revive Tainted Lost after death. This means that items that normally take effect upon taking damage will affect Tainted Lost upon death and revival.
* Beating Delirium with {{C|The Lost}} is not required for Tainted Lost to obtain the {{P|Holy Card}}, or for Holy Cards to spawn during the run.
* As with The Lost, {{r|Devil Room}} items and {{r|Black Market}} items can be taken for free, but will be presented as a choice. Taking one item as a deal will cause the others in the room to disappear.

== Item Exclusion ==
Tainted Lost has two mechanics that determine what items it can encounter.

=== Offensive items ===
The first mechanic makes it so that any items that are not [[Item Tags|tagged]] "<code>[[Item Tags offensive|offensive]]</code>" cannot be naturally encountered while playing as Tainted Lost. This disallows items that it can't take advantage of, similar to {{C|The Lost}}'s {{I|Birthright}}, but it also prevents many powerful defensive items, such as {{I|Dead Cat}} and {{I|Holy Mantle}}, from naturally spawning. These items will be rerolled, and items that are set drops from mini-bosses (ex. {{e|Super Pride}} dropping {{I|Dead Cat}}) will never be dropped.

Disallowed items can only appear by using {{I|Spindown Dice}}, {{I|Death Certificate}}, as set drops from props (ex. {{I|Dry Baby}} from a skull) or Harbingers (ex. {{i|Ball of Bandages}}), or from {{P|Soul of Lilith}}.

Not all items tagged "<code>[[Item Tags offensive|offensive]]</code>" are particularly offense-oriented items. Examples of this include {{I|Treasure Map}} and {{I|The D6}}.

This mechanic seemingly does not work correctly in co-op.

=== Item quality ===
The second mechanic uses the [[item quality]] system. Items with a quality value of 2 or less have a 20% chance of being rerolled when encountered as Tainted Lost. The new item chosen is not guaranteed to have quality over 2.

