== Strategy ==
With only a single {{p|Holy Card}} for defense, defensive items become just as important as offensive ones, as taking more than a single hit in the entire run may prove fatal. However, because all items not marked as "offensive" will automatically be rerolled, defensive options available are less plentiful.

* A good way to secure a powerful run is to visit as many {{r|Boss Challenge Room}}s as possible. It is possible for the player to use the alternate floors to their advantage by sticking to the second floor of each chapter. By visiting {{s|Downpour}} II / {{s|Dross}} II, the player can also get an extra boss item from the [[Mirrored World]]. This strategy comes with the added risk of having to fight more bosses, but provides the potential to snowball the player's stats and make later floors much easier to survive in.
* Be careful of any {{E|Chest|text=Chests}}, which could be a {{E|Mimic Chest}} or a {{E|Haunted Chest}}.
* [[Rocks#Skulls|Skulls]] can be a source of finding cards which in turn can be a {{P|Holy Card}}.
* Waiting before using the {{P|Holy Card}} until after the Shop has been found in case a {{I|Blank Card}} is available for sale can prove helpful.
* Be wary of taking items that automatically attack enemies in case they kill exploding enemies nearby. This includes items like {{I|120 Volt}}, {{I|Demon Baby}}, and items that spawn [[Familiar#Blue Flies|blue flies]].

== Items Interactions ==
=== Favored Items ===
These items provide significant benefits to Tainted Lost.

* {{t|Ace of Spades}}: Chance of changing the room drop reward to a card, and a chance of getting a card as additional rewards from certain things, indirectly increasing the chance of getting a Holy Card.
* {{i|Birthright}}: Grants an extra life, respawning in the same room and damaging nearby enemies.
** This extra life item is the only one that can be naturally obtained as Tainted Lost, as all others are rerolled.
** Taking a hit and using Birthright counts as taking damage and will affect items accordingly, such as losing {{T|Perfection}}.
** Summoning Birthright with {{i|Lemegeton}} will grant infinite lives until the wisp is destroyed.
* {{i|Blank Card}}: Allows a four-charge reuse of the Holy Card.
** {{I|9 Volt}} and {{T|AAA Battery}} each reduce the charge time required by one bar.
** {{I|The Battery}} allows storing an extra use of Blank Card, useful in case you take a hit multiple times in a short period.
* {{I|Bone Spurs}}: Especially useful against enemies that spawn bullets or other enemies on death, as they will often be instantly blocked or damaged/killed, respectively.
* {{dlc|nr+}}{{i|Book of Shadows}}: Very powerful in combination with {{T|Panic Button}} and {{i|4.5 Volt}}.
* {{i|Book of the Dead}}: The Bone orbitals spawned from this item can block projectiles, greatly increasing survivability.
* {{i|Book of Virtues}} / {{i|Lemegeton}}: Rings of wisps can block a lot of projectiles.
* {{I|Booster Pack}}: Has about a 40% chance of spawning a Holy Card.
* {{i|Camo Undies}}: Allows Tainted Lost to be invisible upon entering a room and plan out his first attack.
* {{i|Clear Rune}}: Can be used with protective runes like {{p|Algiz}} or {{p|Soul of Bethany}}. Similarly, {{p|Soul of the Lost}} can be used for a single-use {{I|Holy Mantle}} for the current room.
** {{P|Soul of Lazarus}} also provides a short invincibility streak after reviving.
* {{I|Clicker}}: Becoming Tainted Lost by using Clicker allows Tainted Lost to keep all previously collected items. This allows many useful defensive items that Tainted Lost normally can't collect.
* {{i|Coupon}}: Allows an extra item to be taken from devil deals.
* {{i|Cursed Eye}}: The downside of the item is inconsequential due to Tainted Lost's lack of health.
* {{i|D1}} / {{i|D infinity}} /{{t|Dice Bag}}: Cards duplicated by D1's effect have an increased chance to be Holy Cards.
* {{i|Damocles}}: The downside of the item is inconsequential due to Tainted Lost's lack of health.
** The item can still kill Tainted Lost if resurrected by {{i|Birthright}} or any other acquired respawn item.
* {{I|Dark Arts}}: Provides a powerful panic button to escape swarms of enemies and/or bullets.
* {{i|Deck of Cards}}: Allows more chances for Holy Cards.
* {{I|Death Certificate}}: Tainted Lost can now obtain defensive items, as Death Certificate's item generation ignores Tainted Lost's changes to item availability. This is extremely beneficial, as Tainted Lost can now obtain extra lives such as {{I|Dead Cat}} and protective items such as {{I|Holy Mantle}}.
* {{i|Echo Chamber}}: The next three consumables used after Holy Card will grant another mantle.
* {{T|Endless Nameless}}: Has a 25% chance to spawn another Holy Card when one is used.
* {{t|Flat File}}: Retracts almost all spikes and allows free {{r|Curse Room}} entry.
* {{i|The Gamekid}} / {{i|My Little Unicorn}}: On-demand invincibility with contact damage.
* {{i|Glass Cannon}}: High damage shots that allow the removal of especially dangerous enemies fast. The downside of the item only comes into effect upon the use of a reviving item and not from consuming a Holy Card.
* {{i|Glitter Bombs}}: Bombs may drop a Holy Card when exploding.
* {{dlc|nr+}}{{i|Glowing Hourglass}}: Allows recovery of a Holy Card shield.
* {{I|Guppy's Tail}}: can increase the amount of {{E|Locked Chest}}s found in a run, and thus allows more chances for Holy Cards to appear.
* [[Tear Effects#Homing|Homing tears]]: Allows Tainted Lost to safely position himself almost anywhere in a room while still dealing damage.
* {{I|Little Horn}} / {{i|Euthanasia}}: can destroy almost all "invulnerable" enemies (e.g. {{E|Poky}}, {{E|Stone Grimace}}) before they can hurt Tainted Lost. However, {{E|Ball and Chain}} are still invulnerable and dangerous.
* {{i|Lost Contact}}: Blocks projectiles.
* {{p|VI - The Lovers?}}: Can be safely used to generate items with no loss of durability or risk of death.
* {{i|Mercurius}} / {{t|Door Stop}}: Most rooms can be checked for a safe plan of attack, or bypassed entirely.
* {{t|Missing Poster}}: Allows a one-time revival upon death, respawning Tainted Lost in the previous room.
