=== Disfavored Items ===
These items provide significant drawbacks to Tainted Lost.

* Any explosive tear effect, such as {{I|Fire Mind}} or {{I|Ipecac}}, greatly increases the chance of fatal self-damage. Since {{I|Host Hat}} and {{I|Pyromaniac}} cannot naturally appear as Tainted Lost, there are very few ways to reliably avoid explosive self-damage.
** The same risk also applies for explosive familiars like {{I|BBF}}, {{I|Bob's Brain}}, and {{I|Lil Delirium}}.
** {{I|3 Dollar Bill}}, {{I|Fruit Cake}}, and {{I|Playdough Cookie}} have a chance to shoot {{I|Fire Mind}} tears.
* The [[Stompy]] effect makes firing from cover impossible – all but removing a safe method for Tainted Lost to attack non-flying enemies. Additionally, some obstacles have effects that can cause unavoidable damage if accidentally moved over, such as bomb rocks exploding or blood shots from polyps.
* {{i|Finger!}}: May destroy [[TNT]] accidentally and without warning.
* {{I|Little Baggy}}: Holy Cards will no longer spawn.
* {{I|IBS}}: The effects of poop caused by damaging enemies are completely random, which can lead to an accidental death or loss of a Holy Card.
** Butt bombs may hurt you if you are not paying attention, gas clouds from stinky poop could explode in a chain back to you if thrown at fires, and farts generate a gas cloud that will explode if you are next to a fire, leading to an untimely death.

=== Neutral Items ===
These items can provide both benefits and drawbacks to Tainted Lost.

* Although items which provide temporary invincibility such as {{I|A Pony}} and {{I|Mars}} can allow Tainted Lost to negate damage, their effects are difficult to time, and could result in charging into an enemy and being damaged.
* {{I|Buddy in a Box}}: The familiar's potential tear effects are the same as {{I|Fruit Cake}}, and as such have a small risk of carrying {{I|Fire Mind}} for a floor.
* {{i|Dead Sea Scrolls}}: Can cause items such as {{I|Anarchist Cookbook}} to trigger, potentially causing damage, but may also spawn a Holy Card via {{I|Deck of Cards}}.
* {{I|Experimental Treatment}}: Health is not a factor for Tainted Lost, so it may be included as one of the two stats which are reduced. However, it is more likely to be included as a stat increase, which has no effect.
* {{I|Lemegeton}}: Can give Tainted Lost very useful items, such as {{I|Birthright}}, allowing him to have infinite lives until the wisp is destroyed, but it can also give run-ending items such as {{I|Ipecac}}.  Because Lemegeton's effect is random, this is completely out of the player's control.  If a very bad wisp is gained using Lemegeton, it is recommended to destroy it as soon as possible, but be cautious as this could result in taking damage.
* {{I|Monster Manual}} / {{P|Soul of Lilith}}: Can spawn useful familiars, including some which Tainted Lost cannot encounter normally, such as {{I|Psy Fly}} or {{I|Sworn Protector}}. However, they can also spawn useless or even detrimental familiars, such as {{I|Bob's Brain}} or {{I|Lil Delirium}}.
* {{I|Number One}}: Decreasing maximum range exposes Tainted Lost to danger, but increasing fire rate may make it easier to defeat enemies.
* {{i|Sulfuric Acid}} /{{i|Terra}}: Can skip rooms entirely by breaking doors but also prevent firing from cover.
* {{I|Teleport!}}: Can teleport Tainted Lost away from a dangerous room or before a fatal mistake is made. However, the player can teleport to a {{r|Curse Room}} (or to a Secret Room whose only opened exit is a Curse Room) which is inescapable without a Holy Card.

