== Trivia ==
* While items like {{i|A Dollar}}, {{i|Knife Piece 1}}, and {{i|Knife Piece 2}} are not considered items that the Tainted Lost can find, they will still appear for him if the conditions for finding them are met.
* While [[Harbingers]] will still drop {{i|Ball of Bandages}} or {{i|Cube of Meat}}, {{E|C.H.A.D.}} will not drop {{i|Little C.H.A.D.}}.
* If invincibility is used to play [[Blood Donation Machine]]s, they can still produce a {{i|Blood Bag}} as a reward.
* {{i|Inner Child}} will still spawn in the hidden closet in {{s|Home}}.
* The achievement for unlocking Tainted Lost is "The Baleful", a possible title for the character.
** "Baleful" means "ominous" or "harmful or malignant in intent or effect", possibly referring to how Tainted Lost has higher base damage than his regular counterpart and can find better items.
** A more archaic meaning of "Baleful" is "Something/Someone wretched or miserable", and considering how Tainted Lost is incapable of using defensive heavy builds, being constantly at the mercy of enemies and dying usually at two hits, fit with this use of the word.
** "The Baleful" is Tainted Lost's character name in Four Souls.
* Before the [[V1.7.5|1.7.5 update]], it was possible for Tainted Lost to find {{I|Yuck Heart}} and {{I|Best Bud}}, despite these items being useless for the character.
** Additionally, {{I|Heartbreak}} could be found and utilized to essentially gain 4 extra lives and extra damage, but was removed from the tag list.
* Tainted Lost's unlock drawing could be a reference to a transition nightmare Isaac can have, depicting The Lost talking to {{e|Mom}} from the attic.
* Tainted Lost unlocks {{P|0 - The Fool?}}; the character can be linked to both the numeration and meaning of the Fool.
** The Fool's numeration can be either 0 the lowest trump or 22 the highest trump, linked to his attributes — better items, no mantle, no health — as Tainted Lost will die in a single hit at any point, but can also build the strongest runs of any character because of those same attributes.
** Reverse fool means apathy and nullity; this approach is often recommended to face Tainted Lost's runs because of how demanding the character is and how easy it is to lose these runs despite how powerful the character can become.
** In a literal reversal of "the beginning of the journey" which The Fool represents, Tainted Lost represents the complete end of Isaac's existence, after [[Tainted Forgotten|his own mortal remains]] has vanished and even his own [[The Lost|soul]] erodes into dust and cobwebs along with the house and material objects that hold his last remnant memories.
* Tainted Lost's starting health is listed as "?" on the character selection screen.
* On death, the soul that flies away will be Tainted Lost instead of most other characters having the Lost fly away instead.

